# Thesis Template

What this note is for: the shape of a thesis you consider complete. When you start a position, copy this into `Theses/<TICKER>.md` and fill it. The stress-test and re-test workflows read your thesis notes, extract your load-bearing claims, and check your stated disconfirmers — so the better-structured your thesis, the sharper the test.

## Template (copy to Theses/<TICKER>.md)

```markdown
---
type: thesis
ticker: <TICKER>
company: <name>
opened: <YYYY-MM-DD>
entry_price: <px>
target_weight: <%>
tags: [investing/thesis]
---

# <TICKER> — Thesis

## One-line thesis
<the bet in a sentence>

## How they make money
<plain language; the unit of value>

## The three load-bearing claims
1. <must be true #1>
2. <must be true #2>
3. <must be true #3>
(If you can't get it to three, the thesis isn't clear yet.)

## Why the edge persists (moat)
<source, durability, the evidence>

## Valuation
<what price implies; your conservative value; margin of safety>

## What would make me WRONG (pre-registered disconfirmers)
- <disconfirmer #1 + the observable that signals it>
- <disconfirmer #2 + observable>
(These are sacred. The agent checks whether you quietly drop or redefine them later.)

## Monitoring triggers
<events that should force a re-test>

## Re-test log
- <YYYY-MM-DD> opened
```

> FILL THIS IN — adjust the template to match what *you* think a complete thesis needs. Add fields you care about (capital allocation, key person risk, ESG/regulatory, whatever). Remove what you don't use.
